        <item>
            <title>0.15.37</title>
            <pubDate>Wed, 08 Jul 2026 13:04:22 +0100</pubDate>
            <sparkle:version>198</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>0.15.37</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.2</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <sparkle:hardwareRequirements>arm64</sparkle:hardwareRequirements>
            <description><![CDATA[<ul>
<li>Your own replies no longer go missing or land at the wrong time in the transcript. Corder re-derived the timing of your microphone track and could lay a real phrase onto a silent stretch, where an anti-bleed filter then deleted it. Your track now keeps the transcriber&#x27;s own (reliable) timing, so short replies stay put and stop disappearing. Verified on a real call: a dropped question came back at the right spot and ~40 more of the speaker&#x27;s turns were preserved.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
